# Source evidence is byte-addressed. Never let checkout/add line-ending
# conversion change a recorded receipt or a self-contained snapshot artifact.
corpus/raw/*.html binary
corpus/raw/*.pdf binary
corpus/raw/*.meta.yaml -text
# Every file in a GTFS snapshot is byte-addressed, not just the ZIP. The
# receipt records each extracted member's exact SHA-256 and byte count, and
# `_validate_feed_snapshot` re-reads the member and compares it to the bytes
# inside feed.zip. Nine of the thirteen captured feeds ship CRLF fare tables,
# so with only the feed.zip line here, `core.autocrlf=input` silently rewrote
# CCCTA's fare_attributes.txt from 106 bytes to 104 on `git add` and every
# fresh clone would then fail the check with "retained GTFS file differs from
# the exact ZIP". The whole tree is evidence; none of it is text to normalize.
corpus/raw/gtfs/snapshots/** -text
corpus/raw/gtfs/snapshots/**/feed.zip binary
corpus/snapshots/** -text
corpus/snapshots/**/raw/*.html binary
corpus/snapshots/**/raw/*.pdf binary
